  "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+2 & >-10 \\\\ 2x+2-2 & >-10-2 \\\\ 2x+0 & >-12 \\\\ 2x & >-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & >-12 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & >-\\frac{12}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{2}x}{\\cancel{2}} & >-6 \\\\ x & >-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-6.$",
